# What `railway up` uploads (gitignore syntax). An allowlist: only the studio,
# the package files and the content folders go up. Anything else that lands in
# this folder later (keys, credentials, notes) stays on this machine.

# 1. Ignore everything at the top level...
/*

# 2. ...then let these back in.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/railway.json
!/learnings.md
!/studio/
!/ideas/
!/ventures/
!/projects/
!/research/
!/log/

# From .claude, only the playbook (skills) is shown in the studio.
!/.claude/
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/

# 3. Never upload these, wherever they are (these lines come last so they win).
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.npmrc
.netrc
credentials*.json
.DS_Store
node_modules

# Big work files never go to the Studio (sources, frame caches, Figma scripts).
projects/*/motion/
projects/*/motion-src/
projects/*/figma/
projects/*/figma-scripts/
projects/*/clips/
*.jpg.tmp

# Media never goes up with the code: Railway refuses uploads over ~100 MB.
# The Studio reads renders from its volume (MEDIA_DIR); `npm run publish` sends
# previews, images and audio there with tools/motion/sync-media.mjs. Masters stay
# on this Mac. outputs/ is left out whole, and media files anywhere else too (the
# Studio only serves media from the volume or outputs/, so they'd be dead weight).
# [xX] classes: the match is case-sensitive, so CLIP.MP4 must not slip through.
projects/*/outputs/
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[mM][pP]3
*.[mM]4[aA]
*.[wW][aA][vV]
